module change-frcp87-what-if.grants

import change-frcp-2009-amendment.rule59.{ alter-amend-period-2009 }

/// An emergency declaration grants capabilities for a bounded window and
/// does nothing else (docs/litigate/CHANGE.md §2.7). This one is synthetic
/// (`authoritative = false`): a counterfactual world's layer.
start grants

terminal grants: "A what-if FRCP 87 declaration (no procedure)"

/// For a declared Civil Rules emergency of 90 days (FRCP 87(b)(1)(B)), a
/// court may by order extend the Rule 59(e) time, which Rule 6(b)(2)
/// otherwise locks, "for a period of no more than 30 days after entry of
/// the order" (FRCP 87(c)(2)(A)).
grant rule-59e-emergency on [alter-amend-period-2009] effective [2026-03-02, 2026-05-31) cite "FRCP 87(c)(2)(A)"
{
  unlock
  extend { by court, max 30.days, discretion GoodCause }
}
